# Meta Ads MCP Server Configuration (this fork: stdio only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and fill the values. Never commit `.env` — it is gitignored.
# Start with: node dist/index.js --transport stdio
#
# This fork has no HTTP transport, OAuth login, Firestore, Gemini, Apify or
# URL downloads (ticket 254), so their settings are gone. The keys below are
# the stacksbot design's environment key table (§6.1).

# ── Meta credentials (required) ──────────────────────────────
# The one token every Meta call carries: a system-user token. META_TOKENS
# (named tokens) is not read.
META_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Signs every Graph call (appsecret_proof). Required.
META_APP_SECRET=
META_APP_ID=

# ── Server settings ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Graph/Marketing API version for every Meta call. Optional: the code defaults
# to the version in src/meta/api-version.ts, and tests/meta/api-version.test.ts
# fails if this pin, docker-compose.yml, README.md or deploy.yml drift from it.
META_API_VERSION=v27.0
# Comma-separated tool groups to serve: `<group>` for its read tools,
# `<group>:write` for the rest. Unset serves the read-only default.
META_ADS_TOOLSETS=
# Read server only: "1" refuses any `:write` group.
META_ADS_READ_ONLY=

# ── Write server only (the write guard, ticket 253) ──────────
# The command the fork runs before every non-GET request, and the key it passes
# to that command for its receipts.
META_WRITE_GUARD_CMD=
NOTION_API_KEY=
